Returns the Python library reference on first exposure and incremental Python domain declarations and session symbol table for capabilities relevant to the current `intent`, with declared prerequisites and typed input bindings. Call before `plasm` / `plasm_run`; discovery performs no acquisition or business calls.

Use `session_mode: "new"` with the original intent once per workflow. Later discovery uses `session_mode: "extend"`, the same `logical_session_ref`, and the current need. Intent ancestry supplies context; explicit revisions may replace earlier goals. Existing symbols retain their meaning. Intent does not select the session.

Authorized retrieval and typed graph connections nominate candidates. Jev judges relevance; teaching does not establish necessity, collection membership, task completeness, or permission to execute. Use available teaching and extend for missing capabilities. Write provider and business calls as a Python Program, submit to `plasm`, and execute returned reviewed plans with `plasm_run`.
